# --- Secrets -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Contains your Stripe secret key and the back-office admin key.
# NEVER commit this file. If it leaks, roll the Stripe key immediately.
secrets.local.json
secrets*.local.json
# The kitchen print agent's own config. It holds the print key, which is the
# admin key whenever no dedicated printKey is set — so treat it as a secret.
# The template to copy from is print-agent/config.example.json.
print-agent/config.json

# --- Runtime state (written by the server) ------------------------------------
# Anything the server writes while it runs. New files keep appearing as features
# grow — customers.local.json (loyalty) and discounts.local.json (coupon codes)
# were both missed by the hand-maintained list below, and a list like that goes
# stale silently. So match the whole family: these hold customer names and phone
# numbers and must never be committed.
*.local.json
# The live order board and the owner-edited menu. These are your shop's data,
# not source code — back them up, but don't commit them.
orders.local.json
menu.local.json
# The owner's manual switches: store open/closed and which order channels
# (pickup / dine-in / delivery) are taking orders.
store.local.json
# Queued kitchen tickets. Ephemeral, and it holds the rendered ticket bytes.
print.local.json

# Dated CSV/JSON backups written by the server (startup / daily / periodic /
# shutdown). Contains customer names and phone numbers — never commit.
order-backups/

# --- Dependencies / OS noise ---------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Dev scratch ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Screenshots captured by the CDP browser tests. Handy locally, not worth
# committing — they are regenerated on every run.
_dev/screens/
